  "as_of": "2020-03-23",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would let the Commonwealth guarantee loans to small and medium enterprises where the minister considers this likely to address coronavirus economic impacts.",
   "It would provide up to $20 billion from the Consolidated Revenue Fund to meet Commonwealth liabilities arising from guarantees given to financial institutions.",
   "Rules made by the minister would define eligible enterprises and set guarantee requirements, with the legislation starting the day after royal assent."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Ministerial rules could specify lenders' eligibility, risk sharing, loan terms and maximum loan sizes.",
   "Guarantees could cover loans issued before commencement but after the government's announcement.",
   "The minister could delegate guarantee decisions to the departmental secretary or senior executive staff."
  ],
  "affected": "Small and medium enterprises, authorised deposit-taking institutions, non-bank lenders and the Commonwealth are affected.",
